From 76498c504c07b77a88a5b0a3f2d776372a6ed990 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Adam Cipoletti <adam@amcreativecoach.com>
Date: Sun, 20 Sep 2026 12:21:43 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 58/58] Do not ask the font panel what font the selection is in

Speedometer 3.1 on the PowerBook G4 goes from 0.342 to 0.494, and nineteen of
the twenty suites are now faster than PowerFox. The change is five lines.

-[WebHTMLView _updateFontPanel] exists to tell the shared NSFontManager what
font the selection uses, so that an open Font panel shows the right thing.
Finding out costs a synchronous layout of the whole document:

  _selectionChanged -> _updateFontPanel -> Editor::fontForSelection
    -> styleForSelectionStart -> adjustedSelectionStartForStyleComputation
    -> VisiblePosition::canonicalPosition
    -> Document::updateLayoutIgnorePendingStylesheets

WebKit is careful about this elsewhere: FrameSelection::setSelection defers
the appearance update when a style recalc or a layout is already pending. That
deferral was being defeated, because respondToChangedSelection runs first and
cleans layout on the way.

So a page assigning to input.value in a loop relaid out the document on every
assignment. TodoMVC does exactly that - about two hundred times, against a
list growing to a hundred items - and it was 68% of the ES5 test's main thread
(2835 samples of 4176, 2817 of them inside that one layout call).

Nothing reads the shared font manager unless a Font panel exists, and a panel
that is opened later picks up the selection on the next change. So the whole
thing is skipped when +[NSFontPanel sharedFontPanelExists] is false, which for
a browser with no Format menu is always.

  TodoMVC-Svelte-Complex-DOM   1272 -> 428    TodoMVC-JavaScript-ES5   5332 -> 1947
  TodoMVC-Preact-Complex-DOM   1432 -> 570    ES6-Webpack-Complex-DOM  5616 -> 2238
  TodoMVC-WebComponents        2091 -> 995    TodoMVC-jQuery          10222 -> 6613
  TodoMVC-Angular-Complex-DOM  4197 -> 2974   TodoMVC-React-Complex    3887 -> 2758

The suites that do not type into a text field - the news sites, the charts,
Stockcharts, Perf-Dashboard - are unchanged, which is the expected shape.

This also closes out two pieces of work that the profile had argued for
before this was found: the HTML fast-path parser (parsing was 2.4% of a test
that was 68% waste) and anything aimed at style rule collection or text
measurement, which were 100% and 99% inside the wasted layouts.
---
 Source/WebKitLegacy/mac/WebView/WebHTMLView.mm | 16 ++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Source/WebKitLegacy/mac/WebView/WebHTMLView.mm b/Source/WebKitLegacy/mac/WebView/WebHTMLView.mm
index 3a7e1f3a..284e1df6 100644
--- a/Source/WebKitLegacy/mac/WebView/WebHTMLView.mm
+++ b/Source/WebKitLegacy/mac/WebView/WebHTMLView.mm
@@ -6364,6 +6364,22 @@ static BOOL writingDirectionKeyBindingsEnabled()
     // FIXME: NSTextView bails out if becoming or resigning first responder, for which it has ivar flags. Not
     // sure if we need to do something similar.
 
+    // Everything below exists to tell the shared font manager what font the
+    // selection is in, which nothing reads unless a Font panel has been
+    // opened - and finding out costs a synchronous layout of the whole
+    // document, through fontForSelection -> styleForSelectionStart ->
+    // canonicalPosition -> updateLayoutIgnorePendingStylesheets.
+    //
+    // A page that assigns to input.value in a loop therefore relaid out the
+    // document on every assignment. On Speedometer's TodoMVC-JavaScript-ES5,
+    // which does that about two hundred times against a list of up to a
+    // hundred items, this was 68% of the whole test.
+    //
+    // If a Font panel is ever opened it picks up the current selection on the
+    // next selection change.
+    if (![NSFontPanel sharedFontPanelExists])
+        return;
+
     if (![self _canEdit])
         return;
 
